The Jesus Family Series
This is a record of the genealogy of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah was the father of Perez and Zerah. Tamar was their mother. Perez was the father of Hezron. Hezron was the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of David.
And Jesse was the father of King David. David was the father of Solomon. The mother of Solomon was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Azariah was the father of Jotham. Jotham was the father of Ahaz. Ahaz was the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josias is the father of Jechonias and his brothers. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to leave for Babylon.
After this, the family line continued. Jeconiah was the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Abiud. Abiud was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azor.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Akim. Akim was the father of Eliud.
Elimelech was the father of Elnathan. Elnathan was the father of Ara. Ara was the father of Rakeen. Rakeen was the father of Shallum. Shallum was the father of Jediael. Jediael was the father of Josabad. Josabad was the father of Zeror. Zeror was the father of Tharshish. Tharshish was the father of Kittim. Kittim was the father of Elishah. Elishah was the father of Tarshish. Tarshish was the father of Ahad.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
There were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David until the Jewish people were forced to go to Babylon. And there were 14 from then to the Christ. Jesus Christ was born
Thus the birth of Jesus Christ came about. His mother Mary and Joseph had promised to marry. But before they began to live together, it became clear that she would give birth to a child. She was conceived by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Youssef, was a pious man. He didn't want to shame her in front of people. Therefore, he planned to divorce her quietly.
When Joseph thought about this matter, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said to him, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary as your wife. For the child conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
To have a child. You must give him the name of Jesus. Because he will save his people from their sins.
All this happened so that what the Lord had said would happen. He said it through the prophet,
The virgin will conceive and give birth to a son, and he will be called Immanuel. (Isaiah 7:14) The name Immanuel means "God with us."
Joseph got up from sleep. He did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary into his house as wife.
He did not consummate the marriage until she bore him a son. And Joseph named him Jesus.
The wise men visit Jesus.
Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea. This is the account of the birth of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham. Now
They asked, "Where is the child who was born to be the king of the Jews? For we saw his star when we were in the east, and we have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard about this, he became very angry. Everyone in Jerusalem was also disturbed.
Thus Herod called together all the chief priests of the people, as well as the teachers of the law. He asked them where the Messiah was to be born.
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they answered. "For this is what the prophet has written. He said,
But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah, though you are small among the clans of Judah, out of you will come one who will be ruler over Israel, whose origins are from of old, from ancient times. (Micah 5:2)
And after that, Herod secretly called the wise men. He found out from them exactly when the star appeared.
He sent them to Bethlehem. He told them, "Go! Make a careful search for the child. When you find him, bring me a report. Then I can go and worship him too."
After the wise men had heard the king, they departed on their way. The star which they had seen in the east went before them. And when they had come to the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures, and presented him with gifts: gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
When they saw the star, they were filled with joy.
The wise men went home. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They bowed down and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense and myrrh.
