When the Magi had gone, Joseph had a dream. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. "Get up!" the angel said. "Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is going to search for the child. He wants to kill him."
Joseph got up. In the night, he walked to Egypt with the child and his wife Mary.
They remained there until King Herod died. In this way, the words spoken by the Lord through the prophet were fulfilled. He had said, "I have surely made a choice to bring my son out of Egypt." (Hosea 11:1)
