Jesus is tempted.
The Holy Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness. There, Satan tempted him.
After 40 days and 40 nights without food, Jesus was hungry.
The tempter came to him and said, "If you are the Son of God, command these stones to become loaves of bread."
Jesus answered, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
And then the devil took Jesus to the holy city. And he made him stand on the highest point of the temple.
"If you are the Son of God," he said, "come down from yourself." It is written, "'The Lord commands His angels concerning you, To guard you in all your ways. They will lift you up in their hands, So that you will not strike your foot against a stone.' " (Psalm 91:11,12)
Jesus answered him, "It is also written, 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.' " (Deuteronomy 6:16)
