They came together in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them, "The Son of Man is going to be delivered over to the hands of men."
They will kill him. On the third day, he will rise from the dead." Then the disciples were filled with great sorrow. Jesus saves the temple tax
Jesus and His disciples arrived in Capernaum. There, tax collectors came to Peter. They asked him, "Doesn't your teacher pay the temple tax?"
"Ay, he does," he said. As Peter entered the house, Jesus took the lead in conversation. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. " 'Earthly kings,' " he said, " 'toll taxes and tribute. Do they take these things from their children or from others?' "
"From others," Peter said. "Therefore the children need not pay," Jesus told him.
But what we didn't like was upsetting them. Go to the lake and bait your fishing line. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. You'll find the exact change you need inside. Take it and throw it at them for my tax and yours.
